And indeed there came to them, [the people of Makkah],

from the news (min al-anba'), from the Qur'an, which contains reports of the earlier generations (al-qurun al-khaliyah), or reports of the Hereafter, and what was described of the punishment of the disbelievers,

that which contains a deterrent (muzdajar), a restraining from disbelief. One says: "zajartuhu" and "azjartuhu," meaning "I prevented him." Its original form is "izdtajara," but when the ta' falls after a quiescent zay, it is changed into a dal, because the ta' is a voiceless letter (harf mahmus) and the zay is a voiced letter (harf majhur), so a voiced letter, namely the dal, is substituted for the ta', in order that the two may harmonise. This is at the end of the Kitab of Sibawayh.

Commentary of al-Nasafi (Madarik al-Tanzil) on surah 54, verse 47:

﴿Indeed, the criminals are in error﴾, [i.e., astray] from the truth, in the world;

﴿and madness﴾ [sa'ar], and fires in the Hereafter; or [it means] in destruction and fires.
